UID:suBYF9gNNF47BKlL4UTc4
SUMMARY:CSWGS Gray/Wawro Lecture - Siri Suh
DTSTAMP:20260805T111656Z
DTSTART:20261021T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Center for the Study of Women\, Gender\, and Sexuality  in 
	collaboration with the Department of Sociology at Rice University  invites
	 you to a Gray/Wawro Lecture in Gender\, Health\, and Wellbeing bySiri Suh
	 (https://www.sirisuh.com/)  Associate Professor of Sociology  Brandeis Un
	iversityWednesday\, October 21\, 2026  5:00 PM Reception  6:00 PM Lecture 
	 This event is free and open to the public.&#160\; Advance registration is
	 required.&#160\; The event venue will be confirmed here closer to the dat
	e of the lecture.  Siri Suh is an Associate Professor of Sociology at Bran
	deis University with research interests in the global governance of matern
	al and reproductive health. Her book\, Dying to Count: Post-Abortion Care 
	and Global Reproductive Health Politics in Senegal (https://www.rutgersuni
	versitypress.org/dying-to-count/9781978804548/) (2021\, Rutgers University
	 Press)\, received the 2022 Eileen Basker Memorial Prize for outstanding r
	esearch in gender and health from the American Anthropological Association
	's Society for Medical Anthropology. In 2022\, Suh launched the Into Women
	's Hands (https://www.intowomenshands.org/) project to explore the role of
	 misoprostol in the pharmaceuticalization of reproductive health in franco
	phone Africa. With funding from the Hewlett Foundation\, Suh collaborates 
	with faculty and graduate students at Joseph Ki-Zerbo University in Burkin
	a Faso and Cheikh Anta Diop University in Senegal to conduct ethnographic 
	research on the use and circulation of misoprostol in health facilities\, 
	pharmacies\, informal drug markets\, social media networks\, and with NGOs
	 and professional associations. Suh received her PhD in Sociomedical Scien
	ces and her MPH from Columbia University.&#160\;  Learn more about the Gra
	y/Wawro Lecture Series on our website (https://cswgs.rice.edu/lectures).&#
	160\; This event counts toward the required 12 colloquium events for the C
	SWGS Graduate Certificate.\n\nhttps://events.rice.edu/event/422506-cswgs-g
	raywawro-lecture-siri-suh\n\nFrom Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/event/422506-cswgs-graywawro-lecture-siri-suh
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
